Description: Disable LTO for the vendored bind 9.11.36 build
 bind 9.11.36 (vendored in isc-dhcp) fails to link svtest/dhclient under
 -flto=auto: libisc.a has the symbols (T) but the link still reports
 undefined reference. Strip LTO from both CFLAGS and LDFLAGS.
 .
 This strip used to live in src/isc-dhcp/Makefile as the exports
 DEB_CFLAGS_MAINT_STRIP / DEB_LDFLAGS_MAINT_STRIP set around
 dpkg-buildpackage, which only reached the local self-build. A Launchpad
 builder only ever sees the source package, so the vendored bind would fail
 to link there. Moving the strip into debian/rules makes it apply to the
 local build and PPA builds alike.
Origin: vendor
Forwarded: no
Author: Sheldon Qi <sheldon.qi@canonical.com>
Last-Update: 2026-07-28

--- a/debian/rules
+++ b/debian/rules
@@ -1,5 +1,14 @@
 #!/usr/bin/make -f
 
+# resolute: bind 9.11.36 (vendored in isc-dhcp) fails to link under
+# -flto=auto: libisc.a has the symbols (T), but svtest/dhclient still
+# report undefined reference. Strip LTO from both CFLAGS and LDFLAGS.
+#
+# These two lines used to live in src/isc-dhcp/Makefile as exports set
+# around dpkg-buildpackage -- that only reached local builds; a Launchpad builder only sees the source package.
+export DEB_CFLAGS_MAINT_STRIP = -flto=auto -ffat-lto-objects
+export DEB_LDFLAGS_MAINT_STRIP = -flto=auto -ffat-lto-objects
+
 export DH_VERBOSE=1
 export DEB_BUILD_MAINT_OPTIONS=hardening=+all
 
